<div id="2026-11-18-commit-confirm-drift" class="cl-entry">
<h3>2026-11-18 — AI Editor commit could not be confirmed after a review</h3>
<p class="doc-body"><strong>What.</strong> The AI Editor commit dock (<code>POST /admin/git/editor_commit</code>) reviewed the staged diff and then refused its own review with <em>"The diff changed after review. Review it again before committing."</em> whenever <code>data/ai_trials/*.state.json</code> was staged. The file is rewritten by the app (trial state, spend, timestamps) and re-staged while the review is on screen, so the full-diff hash taken at review time never matched the one recomputed at confirm. Every retry re-read a different hash: the commit could not be completed from that panel at all.</p>
<p class="doc-body"><strong>Why.</strong> Two commit surfaces hashed different things. The Git dashboard gate (<code>_dashboard_commit_gate</code>) hashes <code>strip_data_entry_diff($diff)</code>, so app-written data-entry churn is invisible to it. The editor dock path (<code>_review_for_commit</code> / <code>_confirm_reviewed_commit</code>) hashed the raw diff, data-entry hunks included. It also skipped the data-entry structural check the dashboard runs, so conflict markers or invalid JSON in a staged state file could reach a commit.</p>
<p class="doc-body"><strong>Fix.</strong> The dock path now strips data-entry hunks before hashing, both at review and at confirm, and runs <code>_data_entry_staged_error</code> before reviewing and again before committing. A data-entry-only diff reports "Data-entry files only. Structural checks passed…" instead of looking like an empty diff. Also repaired a wrong assertion in <code>t/util_git_data_entry_commit.t</code> ("data-only diff leaves nothing to review" left a dangling partial <code>diff --git</code> header, so it failed on a correct helper).</p>
<p class="doc-body"><strong>Files.</strong> <code>lib/Comserv/Controller/Admin/Git.pm</code>, <code>t/util_git_data_entry_commit.t</code></p>
</div>
